(20406,'App\\Models\\User',10009,'created','App\\Models\\Protocol',17,'[]','{"Title":"Donepezil Hydrochloride Tablets USP 5 mg and 10 mg","Purpose":"This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies for Donepezil Hydrochloride Tablets USP, 5 mg and 10 mg.","Scope":"this protocol is applicable for long term stability study for below purposes:First three commercial production batches: Long-term Stability Study","Reference":"SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).","Responsibilities":"<p><strong>QC is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.<\\/li><li>Collecting and storing stability samples.<\\/li><li>Labeling of samples.<\\/li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.<\\/li><li>Perform stability analysis.<\\/li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.<\\/li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).<\\/li><li>Initiating change control, deviation\\/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).<\\/li><\\/ul>","ProductID":"10","MarketID":"2","ManufacturerID":"1","AnalysisReport":"Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days.","Reporting":"The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.","Conclusion":"At the end of the long term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.","RevisionHistory":"As Per Change Request #000001220","CreatedBy":10009,"Note":"<ul><li><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong>Current approved version to be followed at the time of execution.<\\/li><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.<\\/li><li>*The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the \\u201cOrganic impurities test\\u201d.<\\/li><\\/ul>","ProtocolID":17}','https://apps.mis.digital/acihc/protocols','192.168.99.2','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/124.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',NULL,'2024-05-06 07:01:33','2024-05-06 07:01:33'),
