(30575,'App\\Models\\User',10009,'created','App\\Models\\Protocol',21,'[]','{"Title":"Gabapentin Tablets USP, 600 mg","Purpose":"This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies for Gabapentin Tablets USP, 600 mg and 800 mg.","Scope":"The scope of this protocol is applicable to below purposes:  \\u2022\\tValidation Batches, Commercial production batches, annual stability batches and batches to be studied for any other reason, e.g. recommended in CAPA, incident, change request. Accelerated stability study is ongoing according to protocol no: 000000725.","Reference":"SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).","Responsibilities":"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>QC is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.<\\/li><li>Collecting and storing stability samples.<\\/li><li>Labeling of samples.<\\/li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.<\\/li><li>Perform stability analysis.<\\/li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.<\\/li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).<\\/li><li>Initiating change control, deviation\\/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>R&amp;D is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Review of the protocol.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Review of the protocol.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>QA is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Review and approval of the protocol.<\\/li><\\/ul>","ProductID":"12","MarketID":"2","ManufacturerID":"1","AnalysisReport":"Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days.","Reporting":"The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation","Conclusion":"At the end of the long term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.","RevisionHistory":"New Revision.","CreatedBy":10009,"Note":"<ul><li>Intermediate (IN) conditions will be withdrawn only if any significant change or OOS found during Accelerated (AC) Study.<\\/li><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.<\\/li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the \\u201c<strong>Related substances test<\\/strong>\\u201d. This Placebo should be used for all strengths (600 mg &amp; 800 mg). The Placebo samples should be withdrawn at each regular time interval.<\\/li><\\/ul>","ProtocolID":21}','https://apps.mis.digital/acihc/protocols','192.168.99.2','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/125.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',NULL,'2024-05-26 05:53:26','2024-05-26 05:53:26'),
