(30634,'App\\Models\\User',10009,'created','App\\Models\\Protocol',35,'[]','{"Title":"donepezil","Purpose":"This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies for Gabapentin Tablets USP, 600 mg and 800 mg.","Scope":"<p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>Note:<\\/strong> Bracketing approach will be applied for stability study of this product. Only 30\\u2019s and 1000\\u2019s count (lower and higher packaging mode) will be applicable for stability study which will cover 90\\u2019s and 500\\u2019s counts also.<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p>","Reference":"SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).","Responsibilities":"<p><strong>QC is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.<\\/li><li>Collecting and storing stability samples.<\\/li><li>Labeling of samples.<\\/li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.<\\/li><li>Perform stability analysis.<\\/li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.<\\/li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).<\\/li><li>Initiating change control, deviation\\/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).<\\/li><\\/ul><p><strong>&nbsp;<\\/strong><\\/p><p><strong>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Review of stability protocol.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>RA is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Review of stability protocol.<\\/li><\\/ul><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p><strong>QA is responsible for:<\\/strong><\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><p>&nbsp;<\\/p><ul><li>Review and approval of the protocol.<\\/li><\\/ul>","ProductID":"16","MarketID":"4","ManufacturerID":"1","AnalysisReport":"Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Stability sample withdrawal from respective stability chambers for testing in sampling due date as (+2 working days from due date for up to 6 months, +5 working days from due date for 9 and 12 months, within +10 working days after 18 months and later time points). Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days after starting of analysis.","Reporting":"The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.","Conclusion":"At the end of the Accelerated or long term or both, stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.","RevisionHistory":"Document Updated as per Change Control: 000001827","CreatedBy":10009,"Note":"<ul><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.<\\/li><li>*The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the \\u201c<strong>Organic impurities test<\\/strong>\\u201d.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<\\/li><\\/ul>","ProtocolID":35}','https://apps.mis.digital/acihc/protocols','192.168.99.2','Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/125.0.0.0 Safari/537.36',NULL,'2024-06-02 04:53:27','2024-06-02 04:53:27'),
