INSERT INTO `Protocol` (`ProtocolID`,`ProductID`,`ProtocolStatusID`,`MarketID`,`ManufacturerID`,`Title`,`Purpose`,`Scope`,`Responsibilities`,`Reference`,`AnalysisReport`,`Reporting`,`Conclusion`,`RevisionHistory`,`CreatedBy`,`CreatedDate`,`UpdatedBy`,`Note`,`FooterSectionNo`,`PreviousProtocolID`,`Reason`,`ExhibitBatch`,`CommercialValidationBatch`,`AnnualStability`,`Other`,`TestNote`) VALUES
(1,38,4,4,2,'Stability Protocol For Febus 80 F/C Tablet','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies for Febus 80 mg F/C Tablets',NULL,'<p><strong>QC is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p><strong>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Review of the protocol.</li></ul><p><strong>QA is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Review and approval of the protocol.</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650 & 000000530)','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Stability sample withdrawal from respective stability chambers for testing in sampling due date as (+2 days from due date for up to 6 months, +5 days from due date for 9 and 12 months  sample and within +10 days for 18 months and  later time). Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study','New Document',10009,'2025-04-20 08:13:27',8,'<ol><li>For Microbial Testing sample should be kept and withdrawn during 24 and 36 months at long term condition.</li><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the “<strong>Organic impurities test</strong>”. The Placebo samples should be withdrawn at each regular time interval.</li><li>Placebo sample has incubated in a container bottle.</li></ol>','000000650/4.00/9.1',NULL,NULL,'Y','N','N','N',NULL),
(2,39,2,5,2,'Stability Protocol for Naftol 25 mg Tablet_BD Market','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies for Naftol 25mg Tablet',NULL,'<p><strong>QC is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p><strong>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Review of the protocol.</li></ul><p><strong>QA is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Review and approval of the protocol.</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Stability sample withdrawal from respective stability chambers for testing in sampling due date as (+2 days from due date for up to 6 months, +5 days from due date for 9 and 12 months  sample and within +10 days for 18 months and  later time). Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study','New Document',10009,'2025-05-29 12:44:28',NULL,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the “<strong>Organic impurities test</strong>”. The Placebo samples should be withdrawn at each regular time interval.</li><li>&nbsp;Microbial enumeration test &nbsp;and test for special microorganisms to be performed &nbsp;initially and yearly at 25°C ± 2°C/60% RH ± 5% RH</li><li>Placebo sample has incubated in a container bottle.</li></ol>','000000650/4.00/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','Y','N','N',NULL),
(3,40,4,2,2,'Azthromycin Tablet USP 250 mg & 500 mg','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies for Azithromycin Tablets USP 250 mg & 500 mg',NULL,'<p><strong>QC is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p><strong>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Review of the protocol.</li></ul><p><strong>QA is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Review and approval of the protocol.</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Stability sample withdrawal from respective stability chambers for testing in sampling due date as (+2 days from due date for up to 6 months, +5 days from due date for 9 and 12 months  sample and within +10 days for 18 months and  later time). Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study','New document',10009,'2025-06-15 08:35:32',10009,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the “<strong>Organic impurities test</strong>”. The Placebo samples should be withdrawn at each regular time interval.</li><li>Microbial enumeration test &nbsp;and test for special microorganisms to be performed &nbsp;initially and yearly at 25°C ± 2°C/60% RH ± 5% RH</li><li>Placebo sample has incubated in a container bottle.</li></ol>','000000650/4.00/9.1',NULL,NULL,'Y','N','N','N',NULL),
(4,41,1,5,2,'CORA-DX F/C Tablet','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies of Cora-DX F/C Tablet, manufactured in ACI Healthcare Limited.',NULL,'<p><strong>QC Personal is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p><strong>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Review of the protocol</li></ul><p><strong>Head of QC or his/her designee</strong></p><ul><li>a. Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>b. Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p><strong>QA is responsible for:</strong></p><ul><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days of due date for up to six months, +5 working days for 9 and 12 months sample, within +10 working days for 18 months and later time points. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days from start of analysis.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long-term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.','New Document',10012,'2025-07-08 12:11:10',10012,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>Microbial&nbsp;test to be done at the initial sample, at the end of the shelf life and in every time point after shelf life.</li></ol>','000000650/5.01/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','Y','N','N',NULL),
(5,42,4,9,2,'Linezolid FC Tablets USP, 600mg/Ezolid 600 FC Tablet','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies of Linezolid FC Tablets USP, 600mg/Ezolid 600 FC Tablet, manufactured in ACI Healthcare Limited.',NULL,'<p>QC Personal is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Review of the protocol</li></ul><p>Head of QC or his/her designee</p><ul><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p>QA is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days of due date for up to six months, +5 working days for 9 and 12 months sample, within +10 working days for 18 months and later time points. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days from start of analysis.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long-term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.','New Document',10012,'2025-07-13 14:51:08',10012,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the “<strong>Organic impurities test</strong>”. The Placebo samples should be withdrawn at each regular time interval.</li><li>Microbial enumeration test and tests for special microorganisms to be performed initially and yearly at 25 ± 2°C/60± 5% RH,&nbsp; 30 ± 2°C/65± 5% RH and 30 ± 2°C/75± 5% RH&nbsp;conditions.</li></ol>','000000650/5.02/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','Y','N','N','test'),
(6,43,4,5,2,'Biocal-DX F/C Tablet','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies of Biocal-DX F/C Tablets, manufactured in ACI Healthcare Limited.',NULL,'<p>QC Personal is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p>Head of QC or his/her designees responsible for:</p><ul><li>To review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>To review&nbsp; and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p>Head of QA or his/her designee is responsible for:</p><ul><li>To review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>To review&nbsp;and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days of due date for up to six months, +5 working days for 9 and 12 months sample, within +10 working days for 18 months and later time points. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days from start of analysis','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long-term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.','New Document.',10012,'2025-07-16 11:02:02',10012,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>Microbial&nbsp;test to be done at the initial sample, at the end of the shelf life and in every time point after shelf life</li></ol>','000000650/5.02/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','Y','N','N',NULL),
(7,44,1,5,2,'Rosetor 10mg & 20mg FC Tablet','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies of Rosetor 10mg & 20mg FC Tablets manufactured in ACI Healthcare Limited.',NULL,'<p><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><p>QC Personal is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p>Head of QC or his/her designee</p><ul><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p>QA is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days of due date for up to six months, +5 working days for 9 and 12 months sample, within +10 working days for 18 months and later time points. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days from start of analysis.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long-term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.','New Document.',10012,'2025-07-20 15:12:40',10012,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the “ Organic impurities test”. The placebo should be withdrawn at each regular time interval.</li><li>Microbial enumeration test and tests for special microorganisms to be performed initially and yearly at 30°±2°C/65±5% RH conditions.</li></ol>','000000650/5.02/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','Y','N','N',NULL),
(8,45,1,9,2,'Rosuvastatin 10mg, 20mg, 40mg FC Tablet','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies of Rosuvastatin 10mg, 20mg, 40mg FC Tablet  manufactured in ACI Healthcare Limited.',NULL,'<p>QC Personal is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p>Head of QC or his/her designee</p><ul><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p>QA is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days of due date for up to six months, +5 working days for 9 and 12 months sample, within +10 working days for 18 months and later time points. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days from start of analysis.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long-term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.','New Document.',10012,'2025-07-23 10:31:05',NULL,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the “ Organic impurities test”. The placebo should be withdrawn at each regular time interval.</li><li>Microbial enumeration test and tests for special microorganisms to be performed initially and yearly at 25°±2°C/60±5% RH&nbsp;, 30°±2°C/65±5% RH &nbsp;&amp; 30°±2°C/75±5% RH&nbsp;conditions.</li><li>This protocol has been prepared for submission purposes.</li></ol>','000000650/5.02/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','Y','N','Y',NULL),
(9,46,1,5,2,'Odazyth 500 FC Tablet (QMS No: 000007752)','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies of Odazyth  500 FC Tablet manufactured in ACI Healthcare Limited.',NULL,'<p>QC Personal is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p>Head of QC or his/her designees responsible for:</p><ul><li>To review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>To review&nbsp; and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p>Head of QA or his/her designee is responsible for:</p><ul><li>To review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>To review&nbsp;and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days of due date for up to six months, +5 working days for 9 and 12 months sample, within +10 working days for 18 months and later time points. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days from start of analysis','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long-term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study','New Document.',10012,'2025-08-06 07:56:21',10009,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>Microbial&nbsp;test to be done at the initial sample, at the end of the shelf life and in every time point after shelf life.</li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the “ Organic Impurities”.</li></ol>','000000650/5.02/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','Y','N','N',NULL),
(10,47,4,4,2,'Febus 40mg F/C Tablet and Febus 80mg F/C Tablet','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies of Febus 40mg F/C Tablet and Febus 80mg F/C Tablet  manufactured in ACI Healthcare Limited.',NULL,'<p>QC Personal is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Review of the protocol</li></ul><p>Head of QC or his/her designee</p><ul><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p>QA is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days of due date for up to six months, +5 working days for 9 and 12 months sample, within +10 working days for 18 months and later time points. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 working days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 working days from start of analysis.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the accelerated and long-term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.','As per Ratification number No: RF/26/015',10012,'2025-08-09 12:11:27',10009,'<ol><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>Submission batch for ROW market</li><li>The Sample shall be incubated as per change control Number: 000001830.</li><li>Microbial test to be done at the initial sample, at the end of the shelf life and in every year after shelf life.</li></ol>','000000650/5.02/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','N','N','Y',NULL),
