(77,128,4,5,2,'Odazyth 500 F/C Tablet (Annual_2026)','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies ofOdazyth 500 F/C Tablet',NULL,'<p>QC Personal is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li></ul><p>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Review of the protocol</li></ul><p>Head of QC or his/her designee</p><ul><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>Is responsible for to review and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p>QA is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>Is responsible for review and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 days from the date of withdrawal.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the  Long-term stability study a summary report shall be prepared with the conclusion on the stability under the packing conditions and terminate the stability study.','New Document',10009,'2026-04-06 09:05:26',NULL,'<ul><li>Additional Study Sample will be pulled out and tested only if needed.</li><li>Microbial &nbsp;enumeration test to be done at initial sample, at the end &nbsp;of the shelf life and in every year after shelf life.</li><li>The Placebo should be subjected to stability studies for the “<strong>Organic impurities test</strong>”. The Placebo samples should be withdrawn at each regular time interval.</li></ul>','000000650/6.00/9.1',NULL,NULL,'N','N','Y','N',NULL),
(78,129,4,5,2,'Biocal-D F/C Tablet (Annual_2026)','This protocol defines the procedure to conduct Stability Studies of Biocal-D F/C Tablet',NULL,'<p><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><p>QC Personal is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Preparation and review of stability protocol.</li><li>Collecting of sample provided by QA and storing stability samples.</li><li>Labeling of samples.</li><li>Initiation and withdrawal of samples.</li><li>Perform stability analysis.</li><li>Preparation of analysis report and trend data.</li><li>Initiating out-of-trend&nbsp;and out-of-specification investigation related to stability analysis (on requisite).</li><li>Initiating change control, deviation/incident related to stability analysis (on requisite)</li></ul><p>VD&amp;LCM is responsible for:</p><ul><li>Review of the protocol</li></ul><p>Head of QC or his/her designees responsible for:</p><ul><li>To review and supervise the compliance with the PSSP</li><li>To review&nbsp; and supervise the compliance with the SOP</li></ul><p>Head of QA or his/her designee is responsible for:</p><ul><li>To review and final approval and to assure adherence to the PSSP.</li><li>Collection and transfer of sample from production to QC.</li><li>To review&nbsp;and final approval and to assure adherence to the SOP</li></ul>','SOP of Stability Designing and Handling of Stability Protocol (000000650).','Analysis will be done as per stability specification and results shall be reported as per respective SOP (Testing and Reporting Result of Stability sample). Sample for testing shall be withdrawn within +2 working days. Stability analysis should be initiated within 10 days from the date of withdrawal and the analysis to be completed within 30 days from the date of withdrawal.','The laboratory raw data shall be reviewed and test results are to be evaluated against the established acceptance criteria. Stability trend analysis shall be reviewed as part of periodic product quality evaluation.','At the end of the  Long